      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "VIDEO AI DENOISE  (FastDVDnet, streaming)\n\n1. On 'Load Video' click  \ud83d\udcc1 Browse this computer\u2026  and pick your clip(s) - the files are used where they are, nothing is copied. (If ComfyUI runs on another machine, use Upload.)\n\n2. Press Run. 'Video AI Denoise' starts in PREVIEW mode: it measures the noise in your video, denoises ~2 seconds from the middle and shows a before|after 100% crop clip on the node, plus a still comparison on the right.\n\n3. Tune strength (1.0 = the measured noise; higher = smoother) and grain (puts some fine grain back). Run again to re-preview. preview_at picks another moment (seconds).\n\n4. Set mode to 'render full video' and Run. The video streams through the GPU frame by frame, so length doesn't matter and memory stays flat. Output: ComfyUI/output/video_denoise/<name>-denoised.mp4 (or .mov for Sony clips with PCM audio), with the original audio, timecode and colour tags.\n\n5. Long renders are saved in 10-second pieces: if you stop ComfyUI (or it crashes), Run again with the same settings and it continues where it stopped.\n\nSeveral clips: select them all in the browser dialog, then '\u25b6 Render all N selected videos'."
      ],
      "title": "How to use",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
